"########################################################################################\n"
"\n"
"■ Alignment with Organizational Mission and Strategy\n"
"\n"
"Formulate a clear answer to \"Why does our company engage in open source?\"\n"
"Linking OSS activities to corporate mission, vision, and business strategy ensures sustained operational commitment.\n"
"\n"
"■ Target Audience Selection\n"
"\n"
"Identify primary reader personas and maintain a consistent tone across the document.\n"
"\n"
"Audience calibration examples:\n"
" * Tech Leads / Architects: Highlight competitive advantages gained through high-quality codebases and modern practices.\n"
" * Project Managers / Line Managers: Present strategic resource allocation advantages through engineering efficiency and talent development.\n"
" * Executives / Budget Owners: Focus on direct business impacts—TCO reduction, risk diversification, and competitive positioning.\n"
" * Staff Engineers: Explain day-to-day productivity gains and professional growth opportunities.\n"
"\n"
"■ Continuous Updates\n"
"\n"
"Treat this document as a living artifact.\n"
"Review and update it regularly as internal OSS adoption matures to reflect fresh case studies and metrics.\n"
